1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,172
Why do headlines get excited about a golden cross?

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:07,811
It's when a fast moving average crosses above a slow one.

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:10,180
It suggests the trend may be turning up.

4
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:15,630
A death cross is the opposite: fast crossing below slow.

5
00:00:15,978 --> 00:00:21,389
But both arrive after much of the move has happened. They confirm a trend, they don't predict one.

6
00:00:21,889 --> 00:00:25,102
Practise with moving averages at memestreet.net.

